  MODEL  (vLLM, shipped)         vllm:time_to_first_token_seconds               ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (vLLM, shipped)         vllm:time_per_output_token_seconds             ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (vLLM, shipped)         vllm:request_queue_time_seconds                ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (vLLM, shipped)         vllm:request_prefill_time_seconds              ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (vLLM, shipped)         vllm:request_decode_time_seconds               ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (vLLM, shipped)         vllm:kv_cache_usage_perc                       ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (SGLang, shipped)       sglang:time_to_first_token_seconds             ILLEGAL
  MODEL  (OTel GenAI semconv)    gen_ai.server.time_to_first_token                   OK
  MODEL  (OTel GenAI semconv)    gen_ai.server.time_per_output_token                 OK
  CLIENT (OTel GenAI semconv)    gen_ai.client.operation.time_to_first_chunk         OK
  TRANSPORT (gRFC A66)           grpc.client.attempt.duration                        OK
  TRANSPORT (gRFC A66)           grpc.server.call.duration                           OK
  TRANSPORT (gRFC A80)           grpc.tcp.sender_latency                             OK
  TRANSPORT (proposed)           grpc.client.attempt.time_to_first_message           OK
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  7 of 14 names cannot be registered as an OTel instrument.
  Every one of them is a MODEL-SERVER name, and the reason is one character:
  ':' is Prometheus namespacing and is not in the OTel instrument charset.

  opentelemetry-sdk raised: Exception: Expected ASCII string of maximum length 63 characters but got vllm:time_to_first_token_seconds
  NB the message says 'maximum length 63 characters'. The name is 32
  characters long. The installed regex is r"[a-zA-Z][-_./a-zA-Z0-9]{0,254}"
  -- correct per spec (255), but the diagnostic points at the wrong thing.

